{
  "method": "Replay selected local+peer+contrarian variants on identical eligible observations with original prior-local-date peers and with peer dates strictly before signal date minus three calendar days. For each version also greedily retain a call only if that asset's previous retained call exited strictly before the new signal. Ties in outcomes are misses. Nonoverlap summaries do not report coverage; calls are selected using outcomes' exit dates for scheduling only.",
  "limitations": [
    "This is a post-selection sensitivity test on the same inspected historical data, not independent or prospective validation. Confidence intervals omit all prior model selection.",
    "Longer delay mitigates but does not establish actual timestamp availability or execution. Peer ranking mixes current asset return with delayed peer returns. Outcome data, benchmark dates and local-time signal assumptions remain unverified point-in-time.",
    "Non-overlap per asset does not remove cross-asset and market-shock dependence, and changes the selected call set. Current-selected universe omits many delisted instruments and filters for observed future outcomes. Yahoo crypto differs from Binance; no execution costs modeled."
  ],
